  'Digital Modeling / CAD / BIM',
  'Digital Modeling / CAD / BIM teaches architecture students to move fluently between precision drafting, 3D modeling, BIM, visualization, parametric workflows, digital fabrication, and presentation. The course emphasizes reliable file habits, geometric accuracy, model intelligence, documentation standards, interoperability, and portfolio-quality communication.',
  $cadbjson${"slug": "digital-modeling-cad-bim", "title": "Digital Modeling / CAD / BIM", "description": "Digital Modeling / CAD / BIM teaches architecture students to move fluently between precision drafting, 3D modeling, BIM, visualization, parametric workflows, digital fabrication, and presentation. The course emphasizes reliable file habits, geometric accuracy, model intelligence, documentation standards, interoperability, and portfolio-quality communication.", "topics": [{"id": "28c018d8-fe1c-486f-8cd4-7b224e842cfa", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Design Workflow, File Hygiene, and Modeling Mindset", "description": "This opening section treats digital work as design infrastructure. Students learn that a beautiful model is only valuable if it is organized, recoverable, transferable, and aligned with its purpose.", "children": [{"id": "9763b25c-59d1-42a2-a6af-1cf9297ed00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital workflow discipline", "children": [{"id": "1e103841-7ef7-4e3a-b89d-d07a79a53e27", "type": "concept", "title": "Folder structure"}, {"id": "09b88669-cfe2-450d-93a6-301713355751", "type": "concept", "title": "Naming conventions"}, {"id": "a666ed98-9e6b-44f4-8ad9-88bcb453d78c", "type": "concept", "title": "Incremental saves and backups"}], "description": "Students build habits that prevent lost work, broken links, mystery units, and chaotic submissions."}, {"id": "6babfe93-5955-4aea-bfed-c7afaadffd06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model purpose and level of detail", "children": [{"id": "834a961e-ecb5-4771-9af1-82bb60dafe15", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept vs. documentation model"}, {"id": "aa097c79-605b-48c3-b3da-ccdcd604ef7a", "type": "concept", "title": "LOD and appropriate detail"}, {"id": "bca5f04c-8405-4267-899a-0eb65ab3cdcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Modeling for output"}], "description": "The goal is to model only what the design question requires, at the right scale and precision."}, {"id": "1f7d5d18-9be5-4591-96d9-1ae3fea4c038", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality assurance mindset", "children": [{"id": "e4574bcf-a7b0-462f-ba5b-a303f71252c4", "type": "concept", "title": "QA checklists"}, {"id": "5c5e6363-9daa-4917-961c-670cac2c2260", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review"}, {"id": "7db46715-6e82-4ce6-b6bb-f2b7837da657", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue tracking"}], "description": "Students learn to check units, geometry, links, exports, and drawings before sharing work."}]}, {"id": "9bcc8cab-ce61-47b7-ad7a-02e9f03fb0d8", "type": "topic", "title": "CAD Foundations: Coordinates, Units, Layers, Linework, and Precision", "description": "CAD teaches exactness. This section makes students fluent in the graphic and geometric discipline needed before BIM or advanced modeling can be reliable.", "children": [{"id": "7ac6e108-09af-426c-81e8-76627ef15e45", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coordinates and units", "children": [{"id": "5921cceb-28fd-4ae5-b261-dd2ee8951db2", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute and relative coordinates"}, {"id": "15743d1e-d528-4126-9b68-cff7a8ebea49", "type": "concept", "title": "Architectural units"}, {"id": "cb280bdb-0b15-46ed-a05f-ad26f0de5594", "type": "concept", "title": "Model space vs. layout"}], "description": "Students learn to draw at true scale and understand model space, paper space, origins, and coordinates."}, {"id": "9363e46d-3c90-4817-a0d5-85922c430fc5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layers and lineweights", "children": [{"id": "e1aaaad6-e4d8-40af-b408-f990bc55d843", "type": "concept", "title": "Layer naming"}, {"id": "f778e185-a9c6-4e71-bfc5-38112fb45545", "type": "concept", "title": "Lineweight hierarchy"}, {"id": "5dd257b4-7441-4d04-b7d2-466939dc64be", "type": "concept", "title": "Color/plot style logic"}], "description": "The point is to make drawings legible, editable, and standards-based."}, {"id": "c49d45c3-02b3-443b-aec2-7600429fdf98", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Precision tools", "children": [{"id": "741753a5-8e8d-429f-bca5-11394e06f6c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Object snaps"}, {"id": "21125eed-e074-414e-9a56-8c1ede56024c", "type": "concept", "title": "Blocks and attributes"}, {"id": "6861235f-231f-41ed-ae62-9680dfc02cdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Arrays and offsets"}], "description": "Students use snaps, constraints, blocks, arrays, and object properties to produce exact geometry efficiently."}]}, {"id": "9f1af667-415c-4aa5-8e8e-eed001702610", "type": "topic", "title": "Architectural 2D Documentation: Plans, Sections, Elevations, Details, and Xrefs", "description": "This section turns drafting skills into architectural documentation. Students learn how plans, sections, elevations, details, and references coordinate as a drawing set.", "children": [{"id": "73c92839-8a37-4d6c-99e5-cadd02c7e531", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Orthographic drawing logic", "children": [{"id": "4c23427e-41b4-42b9-b69d-c4fd1f4e1528", "type": "concept", "title": "Cut plane"}, {"id": "7536134a-7232-4d33-8851-2897713361d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Projection"}, {"id": "9650f9cf-cfb2-415d-83dc-c9ecddabb301", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing hierarchy"}], "description": "Students learn how plans, sections, and elevations describe one spatial proposition from different viewpoints."}, {"id": "e913cd41-1e4b-4d05-93cb-38bd4b8c630a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sheet coordination", "children": [{"id": "43a2751c-be44-46fb-90fe-c50a98e72f83", "type": "concept", "title": "Layouts and viewports"}, {"id": "7fc9ef23-8ae0-4238-8c20-ccf6ae849b15", "type": "concept", "title": "Title blocks"}, {"id": "5b4ccfcf-a483-40a9-b52a-386aab2ad11c", "type": "concept", "title": "Plot settings"}], "description": "Students learn to assemble scaled drawings, viewports, titles, legends, notes, and plotted output."}, {"id": "737bfc16-d735-429a-b318-035c28863b5a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "References and details", "children": [{"id": "592d789c-3f77-46ad-8be7-c213b837bd1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Xrefs"}, {"id": "b95603ca-7f3f-4b0d-a411-5dbf70eab63b", "type": "concept", "title": "Detail callouts"}, {"id": "6cbb63ce-d691-4cff-8add-7540671af85f", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision discipline"}], "description": "The section introduces external references and enlarged detail thinking."}]}, {"id": "386cd9d2-307f-4a06-a7d6-762af39b6398", "type": "topic", "title": "3D Modeling Foundations: Massing, Solids, Surfaces, Components, and Scale", "description": "This section teaches 3D modeling as design thinking. Students learn to build clean models that can be iterated, studied, rendered, exported, and explained.", "children": [{"id": "52022d35-8857-406b-81e8-ee7995c0b111", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Massing and spatial hierarchy", "children": [{"id": "c75600c2-479e-4bd7-95c7-d5273df6dc1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Primitives and booleans"}, {"id": "f73388a7-234e-4877-b8db-7b47eecdce66", "type": "concept", "title": "Groups/components"}, {"id": "87e7c9e2-cee0-4460-b328-82da4894b7a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale and proportion"}], "description": "Students model form, void, site, and program relationships quickly without over-detailing."}, {"id": "c6cd0180-8318-40c8-b27e-19476c448fb5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clean geometry", "children": [{"id": "f4880edb-17aa-47a9-b05e-ed2fa8191285", "type": "concept", "title": "Face orientation"}, {"id": "271ff10f-dc5f-4680-a0d7-54c7827a49e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Groups and nesting"}, {"id": "3aade741-9938-43b4-a7ce-f8be50c32440", "type": "concept", "title": "Model cleanup"}], "description": "Students learn why sloppy edges, reversed faces, stray lines, and non-manifold geometry cause trouble downstream."}, {"id": "28d1f658-b4c8-4153-b81c-e73ffb4babf0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modeling for communication", "children": [{"id": "04fe201d-1d62-4714-846b-2be242728826", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenes and cameras"}, {"id": "eb794760-e257-477f-a99f-33a7b624c87e", "type": "concept", "title": "Section cuts"}, {"id": "f901d37f-7651-4c35-be4b-1c553a1b0c3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploded and analytical views"}], "description": "The goal is to set up scenes, views, sections, and diagrams that make design intent visible."}]}, {"id": "4e191807-c951-498d-9323-c8d3a37442ac", "type": "topic", "title": "Rhino Modeling: NURBS, Mesh, SubD, Curves, Surfaces, and Analysis", "description": "Rhino adds precision and geometric range. This section helps students understand different geometry types and when each supports architectural exploration.", "children": [{"id": "cb9029b0-606e-4539-ac77-dcd995dc6445", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Curves and NURBS surfaces", "children": [{"id": "08b466ce-38dc-4209-a93f-b412dabf86fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Control points"}, {"id": "e2dfca90-772c-45f2-9503-e55d972ce5d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Loft, sweep, revolve"}, {"id": "3721bbeb-72be-413c-8653-2d032313a15e", "type": "concept", "title": "Surface continuity"}], "description": "Students learn to create, edit, and evaluate curves and surfaces for controlled design geometry."}, {"id": "a74b18a1-4d39-4bca-a483-fe2aa6833c7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meshes and SubD", "children": [{"id": "f4d081fc-32f2-441f-a2dd-585a8939ebe7", "type": "concept", "title": "Mesh density"}, {"id": "ac47a118-4d7e-4e2b-983e-ae4512667160", "type": "concept", "title": "SubD form"}, {"id": "6299ab56-214b-4745-880d-77fa03c1754c", "type": "concept", "title": "Conversion tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students understand mesh-based and subdivision modeling for form-finding, exchange, and fabrication constraints."}, {"id": "6b7518c3-e421-43cb-8e97-608c0b085fde", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analysis and export", "children": [{"id": "87cbd1f1-89d7-4594-84e3-4b5d8eedd03f", "type": "concept", "title": "Naked edges"}, {"id": "0f25f2ea-fa9a-4fb6-a874-33f1d70d1ccf", "type": "concept", "title": "Normals"}, {"id": "a3633576-e225-40fc-8fb1-b3a95af3741b", "type": "concept", "title": "File formats and scale"}], "description": "The section teaches geometric checking before rendering, fabrication, or BIM exchange."}]}, {"id": "80076575-e2fd-43ad-b77a-0de745dd794a", "type": "topic", "title": "BIM Concepts and Revit Project Setup", "description": "BIM is not just 3D modeling; it is coordinated building information. Students learn to think in terms of elements, views, parameters, and model governance.", "children": [{"id": "127fbdaa-efbd-46ec-9531-26c487403666", "type": "subtopic", "title": "BIM as model and database", "children": [{"id": "280a704f-306c-42fc-b8f3-e9ae176875ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Categories"}, {"id": "e81ca570-bed4-4c4e-a0bd-2bda6a7ec26d", "type": "concept", "title": "Parameters"}, {"id": "6d0ea1a1-d533-4dfc-9148-84c5a4a3e7ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Bidirectional coordination"}], "description": "Students learn why walls, rooms, doors, views, and schedules are connected information rather than isolated drawings."}, {"id": "be1bac41-2c81-4ecd-896b-5e2f26d7c34a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project setup", "children": [{"id": "2517d106-c762-4c8f-bf3e-fad118d43759", "type": "concept", "title": "Levels and grids"}, {"id": "4212e1cd-97ba-4026-bd51-a66969cb13b8", "type": "concept", "title": "View templates"}, {"id": "00bfa2e1-4aa7-4a57-bcea-614e817f0715", "type": "concept", "title": "Project browser structure"}], "description": "Students establish levels, grids, templates, views, units, and browser organization before modeling."}, {"id": "ac03442b-dfb9-4aee-902b-a92fbddb281c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modeling conventions", "children": [{"id": "e9191a0c-3b17-4a99-9c77-5502a17622c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Naming conventions"}, {"id": "74c86257-d008-4d44-b5c2-6c0413ff64f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Worksets or collaboration concepts"}, {"id": "ca7dd59f-624f-4bcd-a3ef-b6a8757fd8c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Model scope"}], "description": "The goal is to make a Revit model readable to collaborators, reviewers, and future self."}]}, {"id": "35959202-bfab-4af9-9f59-5c82803a598f", "type": "topic", "title": "Revit Building Elements: Walls, Floors, Roofs, Stairs, Rooms, and Assemblies", "description": "This section builds the core architectural model. Students learn how intelligent elements represent actual building systems and drive drawings.", "children": [{"id": "4b071059-079b-401c-a9c2-45003d5c7ba6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core architectural elements", "children": [{"id": "f1a375fb-61dd-4efb-b368-1c8c22e5e404", "type": "concept", "title": "System families"}, {"id": "016def0e-471e-4005-8683-ac4a4a865210", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraints"}, {"id": "ec2b9fab-6c9c-4a17-8253-7f19dd4a98dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Host relationships"}], "description": "Students model walls, floors, roofs, ceilings, doors, windows, stairs, and railings with appropriate constraints."}, {"id": "49c8fd42-2d4d-48da-95a5-6776811d37d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rooms and spatial data", "children": [{"id": "a8f69513-314a-428a-8822-08619ea09e62", "type": "concept", "title": "Rooms and areas"}, {"id": "b273fe93-04f0-484f-b318-1f0f93b9c2c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundaries"}, {"id": "b26b907f-48c9-4b3e-b0a0-1edb18fe6a81", "type": "concept", "title": "Color fills and schedules"}], "description": "Students learn to treat space as measurable information, not just empty volume."}, {"id": "5633d3e2-0b5d-4910-b488-5d672dbb10ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assemblies and constructability", "children": [{"id": "a9af26f6-a546-40f7-88db-9345f75d2863", "type": "concept", "title": "Wall build-ups"}, {"id": "13c29ea3-ec88-4f02-b085-73bc2c99f84a", "type": "concept", "title": "Joins and intersections"}, {"id": "5411d313-013c-4e15-94ff-efdffa17f083", "type": "concept", "title": "Basic detailing implications"}], "description": "The section links model elements to materials, layers, interfaces, and realistic building logic."}]}, {"id": "ccdb6e3c-0b40-46cb-9476-ff4136734ab9", "type": "topic", "title": "Families, Components, Parameters, Materials, and Schedules", "description": "Reusable, data-rich content is where BIM becomes powerful. This section introduces parametric families and schedules as tools for design control.", "children": [{"id": "bb1906f4-22f9-4e7c-b5b1-e2bc016aa6eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Families and components", "children": [{"id": "96a7c2b7-9db9-4234-8a28-2a56536646c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Family categories"}, {"id": "8f64a248-3b69-4433-9823-b635c60a2d68", "type": "concept", "title": "Type vs. instance"}, {"id": "2de03860-d840-4c63-b32a-c74285bfb920", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference planes"}], "description": "Students learn how loadable and system families shape content, standards, and model consistency."}, {"id": "2688fc76-dd4d-4ff2-ad21-e1a73b33dadc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Parameters and materials", "children": [{"id": "356ac6d1-4c15-4143-b10f-c8a6d67399ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared parameters"}, {"id": "2f12b976-5196-4dce-aff1-aed7d6feff33", "type": "concept", "title": "Material assets"}, {"id": "80ad6144-81d3-4c3c-815e-3d246b94b75b", "type": "concept", "title": "Naming and classification"}], "description": "Students attach meaningful data to objects for documentation, analysis, and scheduling."}, {"id": "9abff845-fdad-4b46-bfb2-e8a5ac36500e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Schedules", "children": [{"id": "349247bc-96c6-4fbe-95b6-c66a02da5b20", "type": "concept", "title": "Schedule fields"}, {"id": "9f2bd943-4fc0-420e-b010-d22e708ea58a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sorting and filtering"}, {"id": "a60c0817-23ec-4474-b142-bdba9c4f330b", "type": "concept", "title": "Calculated values"}], "description": "The section shows how model data becomes quantities, room lists, door schedules, and QA tools."}]}, {"id": "02a38b84-aca0-403f-9fdf-61f4069c42be", "type": "topic", "title": "BIM Documentation: Views, Annotation, Tags, Sheets, Details, and Issue Sets", "description": "Students learn to produce coordinated drawing sets from a live model. The emphasis is legibility, standards, and drawing control.", "children": [{"id": "72b623fe-22ac-4e11-8522-c518889a5619", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Views and graphics", "children": [{"id": "dcda07d8-abae-43e3-8736-6576b4978906", "type": "concept", "title": "View ranges"}, {"id": "54d8f4d8-76cf-4e37-b01f-11f83d046604", "type": "concept", "title": "Filters"}, {"id": "3dddb1ac-d8a6-41c7-bfe6-90297c174a31", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphic overrides"}], "description": "Students manage plans, sections, elevations, 3D views, view templates, filters, and visibility settings."}, {"id": "5845e4fe-d3f0-412d-80e6-57dcfaacf7c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Annotation and tags", "children": [{"id": "dbe72d42-4d97-475f-890e-8544584abe0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Dimensions"}, {"id": "f23b2ce4-becd-4938-ba0e-43f1c49a6755", "type": "concept", "title": "Tags"}, {"id": "0e205a1a-6149-4bec-88f3-efaf5d6efe40", "type": "concept", "title": "Keynotes and notes"}], "description": "Students annotate BIM output with dimensions, tags, keynotes, detail callouts, and text standards."}, {"id": "48c25389-be25-4d9a-9d70-4f9017827d56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sheets and issue sets", "children": [{"id": "5615ba18-c60f-4c21-a517-658831f0aa04", "type": "concept", "title": "Sheet indexes"}, {"id": "14c39d7f-d6b3-4c1a-8b24-89d9430fb35d", "type": "concept", "title": "PDF/export settings"}, {"id": "59cfaddf-4a5f-440a-bfdd-7ff672bd9cc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision clouds and logs"}], "description": "The section teaches sheet layout, revisions, exports, and submission discipline."}]}, {"id": "1809ee68-a69c-4c29-ab11-2e6924943da6", "type": "topic", "title": "Interoperability: DWG, IFC, Linked Models, Coordinates, and Model Exchange", "description": "Architecture work moves between tools and teams. This section teaches students to exchange models without corrupting scale, coordinates, data, or authorship.", "children": [{"id": "bb28569c-a2c7-4eb5-99a6-71a4b502a975", "type": "subtopic", "title": "File formats and exchange", "children": [{"id": "a1a808fb-645d-4010-8e38-2cace782338d", "type": "concept", "title": "Import/export settings"}, {"id": "98a23270-74c2-48be-9807-39053f6c8a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometry vs. data"}, {"id": "b618ff4c-b128-4bbd-9fdc-83d501967181", "type": "concept", "title": "Round-trip risks"}], "description": "Students learn when to use DWG, RVT, SKP, 3DM, OBJ, FBX, IFC, PDF, and image formats."}, {"id": "0fe92860-c380-4476-96dc-dfad0c192b8b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coordinates and linking", "children": [{"id": "621d7ee8-b6f3-48e6-8fc5-178a3e57ba84", "type": "concept", "title": "Survey/project base points"}, {"id": "fc979dca-cbc1-4c43-8976-917a5032293f", "type": "concept", "title": "Linked files"}, {"id": "0ea973ac-18d7-4cdf-b2f6-55a87e4a2ef8", "type": "concept", "title": "Path management"}], "description": "Students understand origins, shared coordinates, linked models, underlays, and reference management."}, {"id": "e0af7cf6-c205-4aea-9613-43bfa2bda821", "type": "subtopic", "title": "OpenBIM and IFC", "children": [{"id": "fecb2dd2-39ba-4864-94eb-ae7fa3234ade", "type": "concept", "title": "IFC schema basics"}, {"id": "f4787a1e-9166-4e27-abe3-817336219b3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Model view definitions"}, {"id": "321a36d5-f6fc-42ca-a286-9863f4a7e8c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Validation and QA"}], "description": "The section introduces vendor-neutral model exchange and why data validation matters."}]}, {"id": "281c2a2e-2112-4dd4-b524-76c7598c553f", "type": "topic", "title": "Visualization: Materials, Lighting, Cameras, Rendering, Post-Production, and Storytelling", "description": "Visualization is argument, not decoration. Students learn to create images that clarify atmosphere, material, spatial sequence, and design intent.", "children": [{"id": "931e81a4-c536-4210-8016-e0b49fa08b71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materials and lighting", "children": [{"id": "ebcf1da5-12bb-40da-ad0f-54de9836737d", "type": "concept", "title": "Material maps"}, {"id": "38877849-8d66-4fe1-961a-cea1b0e82872", "type": "concept", "title": "Sun studies"}, {"id": "6fb09013-d113-47fb-a94b-0c828c99536c", "type": "concept", "title": "Interior and exterior lighting"}], "description": "Students tune material properties, daylight, artificial light, exposure, and environmental context."}, {"id": "9389cad0-7309-49e1-81b2-8f5b3e7a0aa8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cameras and composition", "children": [{"id": "d86f8f21-ea62-4f21-b3c3-3808f13ab45d", "type": "concept", "title": "Perspective control"}, {"id": "773bea19-c7a5-43cf-b2b4-fdfd297967a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene setup"}, {"id": "864be776-d87c-4634-ab35-6083fd6f0a66", "type": "concept", "title": "Human scale"}], "description": "Students learn viewpoint, lens, crop, entourage, and depth as design communication choices."}, {"id": "abbe6254-1bdd-460c-8811-9e68c0195c37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post-production ethics", "children": [{"id": "a8bc79a9-7624-48e2-92a6-a8e56502ef15", "type": "concept", "title": "Photoshop workflow"}, {"id": "8056e043-395e-47a3-8de2-e595698a5437", "type": "concept", "title": "Diagram overlays"}, {"id": "212617d6-cc89-4c18-b01c-009fbe9391ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding misleading images"}], "description": "The section covers image correction, diagrams, overlays, and truthful enhancement."}]}, {"id": "54bbf62b-6ef8-4175-8fa8-44f91846cadb", "type": "topic", "title": "Adobe and Presentation Workflows: Photoshop, InDesign, Boards, Portfolios, and Accessibility", "description": "A good digital model still needs clear presentation. This section turns exports into professional boards, portfolios, and accessible PDFs.", "children": [{"id": "6d467a09-91af-4ad8-9aa6-b619d102b532", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image editing workflow", "children": [{"id": "18b60bd1-73b7-4880-8a0b-4f92ac54d778", "type": "concept", "title": "Layers and masks"}, {"id": "9dc9f482-e1c7-466f-9325-a1161a50c94a", "type": "concept", "title": "Color correction"}, {"id": "41ebe0c6-ed60-4dfb-8f87-c82eb61f1ca9", "type": "concept", "title": "Resolution and file types"}], "description": "Students refine renderings, diagrams, scans, and exported linework while preserving quality."}, {"id": "fd590fd3-86e6-4d99-a54e-65d3384ab226", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layout and hierarchy", "children": [{"id": "3d60279e-9c03-466b-b1fb-3838d370b7a9", "type": "concept", "title": "InDesign grids"}, {"id": "588e4e2e-c8d5-4a25-a584-b5430e0ba38e", "type": "concept", "title": "Type hierarchy"}, {"id": "a1c93485-66b0-4883-bae5-8ae5ac24413a", "type": "concept", "title": "Board composition"}], "description": "Students learn typography, grids, alignment, captions, sequencing, and visual hierarchy."}, {"id": "223510ba-32ea-4424-9829-ff0556989273", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Export and accessibility", "children": [{"id": "e49e667e-9132-45fd-9b4d-b5298fb9dfcb", "type": "concept", "title": "PDF export"}, {"id": "0de11c28-d47b-4719-9839-493159e31493", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and readable type"}, {"id": "b7f151bb-a42e-4092-86ec-cf1d8f0992e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Package and archive files"}], "description": "The section covers print/digital export settings and inclusive communication."}]}, {"id": "ef04b64f-7ea5-4c9b-9db6-fae1b8642a58", "type": "topic", "title": "Parametric Modeling with Grasshopper and Dynamo", "description": "Parametric tools teach students to design relationships rather than isolated shapes. This section introduces visual programming for architecture.", "children": [{"id": "b15455f3-8acf-4d57-b14b-f4327084d8d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Computational design basics", "children": [{"id": "a41f3204-2a74-4160-83d5-cb4cef9e1e05", "type": "concept", "title": "Parameters"}, {"id": "9a579d0a-e02b-4803-9b44-ac9408a57faa", "type": "concept", "title": "Functions"}, {"id": "a648b975-3329-4b91-95da-6e6cf98a347d", "type": "concept", "title": "Design variables"}], "description": "Students learn parameters, inputs, outputs, sliders, functions, and algorithmic thinking."}, {"id": "21492a85-4722-4fd0-bc15-1732bc4d429e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grasshopper data and geometry", "children": [{"id": "e1fd6bdf-d090-40f1-9246-f4fe7a74c75d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lists and data trees"}, {"id": "f41e7b4d-4094-4b4a-b3e3-ad39667107aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometric operations"}, {"id": "f2b8c675-928d-4d5f-910e-d160b9f3d4cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Panelization"}], "description": "Students manipulate lists, trees, curves, surfaces, panels, and attractor systems."}, {"id": "f62e46d1-74bb-4c85-8f32-ef051b301648", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dynamo and BIM automation", "children": [{"id": "63bc6db0-0eae-48d7-8ec2-915775eccd82", "type": "concept", "title": "Element selection"}, {"id": "4fc9fff0-3828-4d6b-a62d-17e6aa5bb672", "type": "concept", "title": "Parameter updates"}, {"id": "628097d0-7156-405a-a3fd-89ceecfdf9c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Excel import/export"}], "description": "The section connects visual programming to Revit data, elements, parameters, and Excel workflows."}]}, {"id": "50f0f344-b10d-431e-9888-be56a34c1480", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Fabrication: Laser Cutting, CNC, 3D Printing, File Prep, Tolerances, and Prototyping", "description": "Digital fabrication reveals whether the model can become material. Students learn to prepare geometry for machines, materials, time, and tolerances.", "children": [{"id": "04cac7d5-9434-4695-a7df-2592518b1a75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fabrication methods", "children": [{"id": "f6ce51c7-ec85-4206-bc56-f1690365c11a", "type": "concept", "title": "Subtractive vs. additive"}, {"id": "d6e96773-3969-410e-bf29-99df881d9f24", "type": "concept", "title": "2D profiles"}, {"id": "412f1e00-fce0-460e-a14f-00fa1ab03d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Layering and assembly"}], "description": "Students compare laser cutting, CNC routing, 3D printing, and hybrid model-making."}, {"id": "06ff2920-19fe-4926-b7fe-f27d2498189f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "File preparation", "children": [{"id": "eba2dd5e-5245-4a38-ae2d-707630527a47", "type": "concept", "title": "Closed curves"}, {"id": "c19fcc59-d100-4bf5-aa37-82b89f3376b4", "type": "concept", "title": "STL mesh checks"}, {"id": "6e12f6e0-5869-44e2-8830-22d4cb828487", "type": "concept", "title": "Nesting and kerf"}], "description": "Students prepare clean vectors, meshes, solids, nesting layouts, and machine-ready exports."}, {"id": "d80c8f37-2d0e-4b02-a15b-73b175bedc39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tolerance and prototyping", "children": [{"id": "db1be687-d653-49cc-ad79-8dfff9de91f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Material thickness"}, {"id": "8c12a6ca-2047-48a4-9d69-6dc13829908b", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint tests"}, {"id": "e279f78f-4c09-4d0e-95aa-cf54015dbd2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototype feedback"}], "description": "The section teaches iteration through material tests and assembly details."}]}, {"id": "d0b035bb-a8e8-4a31-8010-c98aa6da1c53", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Capstone: Coordinated Digital Building Model, Documentation, Visualization, and QA", "description": "The capstone asks students to move across the whole digital ecosystem with purpose. The deliverable is a coordinated, reviewable, portfolio-ready workflow rather than a pile of unrelated files.", "children": [{"id": "b9540eb2-8676-452c-a791-8f13fdde0452", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated model package", "children": [{"id": "df220071-8549-42ff-b8c9-ac9795963bc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Model organization"}, {"id": "946a78a6-6513-43c9-913a-1e33a32fc4de", "type": "concept", "title": "Linked references"}, {"id": "62faf7cc-b6dc-4abb-afcc-b9468ccee889", "type": "concept", "title": "Deliverable scope"}], "description": "Students coordinate CAD/BIM/3D components into a coherent building proposition."}, {"id": "527507e4-0ae2-4165-bc88-6eca8615e84b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation and visualization set", "children": [{"id": "9466079a-038d-4c17-b82c-cdafd3262656", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans/sections/elevations"}, {"id": "a3971461-e099-4152-a477-43f6bfa17253", "type": "concept", "title": "Schedules"}, {"id": "887b1d50-998e-4994-bfad-ca540b4652b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation boards"}], "description": "Students produce drawings, schedules, renderings, diagrams, and boards from coordinated source files."}, {"id": "007b7eb4-f936-417d-aaeb-b6693c072df2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "QA and reflection", "children": [{"id": "97f9282a-17d0-4df3-8509-a63deb3c016e", "type": "concept", "title": "QA checklist"}, {"id": "50d3d522-049a-40fb-a662-3f4474f5db61", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow reflection"}, {"id": "7e2b4937-595d-4c60-a4f1-9549a0822467", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio export"}], "description": "The final step makes students audit files and explain their digital decisions."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$cadbjson$::jsonb,
